Falsifies `page_frames::verification::bitmap_bytes_covers_every_frame`.

The defect: the bitmap is sized by floor division, `frames / 8` in place of `frames.div_ceil(8)`.
It is the commonest sizing error there is: the two spellings agree on every multiple of eight,
which is every number anyone types into a test. Milestone 323 (the falsification record is
incomplete in five ways) injected the same defect into `align4`, one crate over.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(bitmap_bytes(frames) * 8 >= frames)`, for any frame
count not a multiple of eight, where the last few frames have no bit and `get`/`set` index past
the end of the bitmap.

diff --git a/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs b/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
@@ -154,3 +154,3 @@
     pub const fn bitmap_bytes(frames: usize) -> usize {
-        frames.div_ceil(8)
+        frames / 8
     }
